        "payload": "tree 2ef25e5d0deb4b7579badda156f510348dff49ac\nparent 9f63ed76c4127ba31cb5b0f0263d3217293953ab\nauthor Meylis <meylis@divine.video> 1779938291 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779938291 +0500\n\nfix(notifications): preserve normalized payload on foreground local notification taps (#4728) (#4757)\n\n* fix(notifications): preserve normalized payload on foreground local notifications (#4728)\n\nForeground FCM banners displayed a local notification via sendLocal()\nwithout a tap payload, so tapping a foreground-generated notification did\nnothing — the shared router from #4727 had no context to route with.\n\n- Extract localNotificationTapPayload() as the single source of truth for\n  the local-notification tap payload shape (referencedEventId, eventId,\n  notificationType, senderPubkey). The background/system-push handler and\n  the foreground handler now both build it, so they cannot drift.\n- sendLocal() gains an optional payload param, threaded to the plugin's\n  show(payload:).\n- handleForegroundMessage() attaches the normalized payload, so foreground\n  taps (including follow/mention, which carry no referencedEventId) route\n  through the same contract as background/system-push taps.\n\nTests pin the payload shape and a round-trip from the foreground payload\nthrough the real tap handler to a routable NotificationTapEvent.\n\n* refactor(notifications): centralize tap-payload keys, derive writer from parser\n\nAddresses self-review of #4757. The local-notification tap payload had its\nfield names hand-mirrored across the writer (localNotificationTapPayload) and\ntwo readers, so the \"cannot drift\" guarantee only held for the two writers.\n\n- Extract NotificationPayloadKeys as the shared key vocabulary; reference it\n  from parseFcmPayload and the writer.\n- Build localNotificationTapPayload by running data through parseFcmPayload so\n  it shares the readers' empty-string normalization instead of re-deriving it.\n\nNo routing behavior change; empty wire fields now normalize to null on the\nlocal payload too (the readers already treated empty and absent identically).\n\n* fix(notifications): route local-notification taps on cold start (#4728)\n\nForeground/background paths now attach a tap payload, but the consumption side\nonly wired FCM getInitialMessage — which covers OS-rendered pushes (iOS, where\ndivine-push-service's synthesized APNS alert is shown by the OS) but not\napp-rendered local notifications. The service sends data-only messages, so on\nAndroid every push is rendered locally by flutter_local_notifications and a tap\nthat launched the app from a *terminated* state was silently dropped:\ngetNotificationAppLaunchDetails was never consulted.\n\n- Add NotificationService.takeLaunchNotificationTap(), consulted once at startup\n  next to getInitialMessage in main.dart, routing any launch payload through the\n  shared _routeNotificationTap.\n- Extract _parseTapPayload so the live-tap and cold-start paths share one parser.\n- Inject the plugin behind a @visibleForTesting seam (debugConfigurePlugin) so\n  sendLocal(payload:) -> show(payload:) forwarding and the cold-start path are\n  unit-tested — the prior round-trip test bypassed both.\n\nSatisfies the cold-start acceptance criterion of #4728.",
